# Changelog

## Unreleased

### Added
- New shared-library step `gitlabGetRepositoryTree` in `vars/gitlabGetRepositoryTree.groovy`.
  - Lists the files and directories of a GitLab repository via `GET /projects/:id/repository/tree`, returning GitLab's own entry shape (`id`, `name`, `type`, `path`, `mode`).
  - Derives the project and the host from `env.GIT_URL` by default, so a build of the repository it inspects calls it without arguments; `projectId` plus `gitlabBaseUrl` address any other project.
  - Supports `path`, `ref` and `recursive`, plus `credentialsId`, `pageSize`, `maxPages` and `debug`.
  - Walks every page of the endpoint instead of returning the first one, and fails rather than returning a silently truncated tree once `pageSize * maxPages` entries are exceeded.
  - Reports a status of 400 or above through `error(...)` with the URL and the credentials ID, so a missing ref or an unauthorised token names itself.
- Step documentation in `vars/gitlabGetRepositoryTree.txt` and unit tests in `src/test/groovy/vars/GitlabGetRepositoryTreeTest.groovy`.
- Map-notation Jira steps, all named with the `jira` prefix, replacing the legacy positional ones:
  - `jiraGetIssueInfo(issueKey:, credentialsId:)` — replaces `getJiraIssueInfo`.
  - `jiraGuessIssueInfo(credentialsId:)` — replaces `guessJiraIssueInfo`.
  - `jiraAddRemoteIssueLink(url:, issueKey:, title:, credentialsId:)` — replaces `addJiraIssueLink`; resolves the issue from the MR title when `issueKey` is omitted, builds the request body with `JsonOutput` and posts to the remote-link endpoint directly, without the extra issue lookup.
  - `jiraCreateVersion(version:, projectKey:)` — replaces `createNewJiraVersion`.
  - `jiraAssignFixVersionToIssues(version:, projectKey:, statusName:)` — replaces `assignJiraFixVersion`, named apart from the single-issue `jiraAddFixVersion`.
  - Step documentation for each of them in `vars/jira*.txt`.
- Unit tests for remote-link creation in `src/test/groovy/vars/JiraAddRemoteIssueLinkTest.groovy`.
- Unit tests pinning the signatures of the deprecated wrappers in `src/test/groovy/vars/DeprecatedJiraStepsTest.groovy`.
- New shared-library step `jiraGetIssueComments` in `vars/jiraGetIssueComments.groovy`.
  - Reads the comments of an issue via `GET /rest/api/2/issue/:key/comment` and walks every page, so the thread of a long-running ticket is not cut at Jira's page size.
  - Resolves the issue key from the MR title via `jiraGuessIssueInfo` when `issueKey` is omitted.
  - Supports `orderBy`, `expand`, `limit` (which also shrinks the requested page size) and `pageSize`, plus `credentialsId` and `DEBUG`.
  - Treats an empty body as an anomaly and throws: an issue without comments still answers with a page carrying `comments: []`.
- `jiraGetIssueInfo(issueKey:, withComments: true)` returns the issue together with its whole comment thread in `fields.comment`, read through `jiraGetIssueComments`. The issue endpoint alone carries a single page of comments.
- Step documentation in `vars/jiraGetIssueComments.txt`, and the `withComments` option in `vars/jiraGetIssueInfo.txt`.
- Unit tests in `src/test/groovy/vars/JiraGetIssueCommentsTest.groovy` and `src/test/groovy/vars/JiraGetIssueInfoTest.groovy`.

### Changed
- `jiraGetIssueInfo` reads the response body through `response?.content` instead of `response.getContent()`, matching the other `jira*` steps.
- `reportUsage` logs `WARNING: <step>() is deprecated` in the build log when it is called with a truthy `deprecated` argument; a String value names the replacement step in the warning and becomes the value of the `deprecated` tag.
- The Jira steps and the build steps of the library call the new `jira*` steps, so they no longer emit deprecation warnings.
- `jiraTransitionIssueToValidation`, documented as deprecated since it was added, now warns in the build log of every pipeline that still calls it.
- `jiraAssignFixVersionToIssues` escapes the status name in the JQL it builds, so a status such as `Client's review` no longer breaks the query.
- A title made of whitespace falls back to the last segment of the URL in `jiraAddRemoteIssueLink` (`addJiraIssueLink` did it for an empty title only).
- `addJiraIssueLink` posts the link to `/rest/api/2/issue/<issueKey>/remotelink` through the new step instead of to the `self` URL of the fetched issue. Both address the same issue, one Jira call less; a Jira whose configured base URL differs from `jira.spacebridge.com` would be reached at the latter now.
- `README.md` also lists `jiraKeyFromTitle` and `jiraTransitionIssue`, which were missing from the Jira section.

### Deprecated
- `addJiraIssueLink`, `assignJiraFixVersion`, `createNewJiraVersion`, `getJiraIssueInfo` and `guessJiraIssueInfo` are kept as thin wrappers over the new steps for backward compatibility. They report `deprecated` to the usage statistics and warn in the build log.
- `jiraTransitionIssueToValidation`, already documented as deprecated, now reports it too.
- New shared-library step `jiraGetRemoteIssueLinks` in `vars/jiraGetRemoteIssueLinks.groovy`.
  - Lists the remote links of a Jira issue via `GET /rest/api/2/issue/:key/remotelink` — the links created by `addJiraIssueLink`.
  - Resolves the issue key from the MR title via `guessJiraIssueInfo` when `issueKey` is omitted.
  - Supports `titleContains` and `url` filtering, so a duplicate check before adding a link is a single call, plus `credentialsId` and `DEBUG`.
- Step documentation for `jiraGetRemoteIssueLinks` in `vars/jiraGetRemoteIssueLinks.txt`.
- Unit tests for remote-link listing behavior in `src/test/groovy/vars/JiraGetRemoteIssueLinksTest.groovy`.
- New shared-library step `gitlabUpdateFile` in `vars/gitlabUpdateFile.groovy`.
  - Updates a single existing repository file via `PUT /repository/files/:path`, creating one commit on the target branch.
  - Derives project/base URL from `gitUrl` or accepts an explicit `projectId`; sends content as a JSON body with `PRIVATE-TOKEN` auth.
  - Validates required inputs (`filePath`, `content`) and supports `branch`, `commitMessage`, author overrides, and `debug`.
- Step documentation for `gitlabUpdateFile` in `vars/gitlabUpdateFile.txt`.
- Unit tests for file-update behavior in `src/test/groovy/vars/GitlabUpdateFileTest.groovy`.
- New shared-library step `addConfluenceComment` in `vars/addConfluenceComment.groovy`.
  - Adds a comment to a Confluence page by `PAGE_ID`.
  - Supports `RAW` response mode and `DEBUG` logging mode.
  - Validates required inputs (`PAGE_ID`, `COMMENT`) and returns actionable errors.
- Step documentation for `addConfluenceComment` in `vars/addConfluenceComment.txt`.
- Unit tests for comment creation behavior in `src/test/groovy/vars/AddConfluenceCommentTest.groovy`.
- Unit tests for GitLab tag/release behavior in `src/test/groovy/vars/TagToGitlabTest.groovy`.

### Fixed
- Fixed `tagToGitlab` GitLab API flow in `vars/tagToGitlab.groovy` to prevent `400 Bad Request` when recreating tags with release notes.
  - Switched from query-string `private_token` to `PRIVATE-TOKEN` request header.
  - Added safe fallback: if `POST /repository/tags` with `release_description` returns `400`, retry tag creation without `release_description`.
  - Removed release deletion/recreation calls that could fail with `403` for limited tokens.
  - Added idempotent `400` handling: when GitLab says tag creation failed, the step checks existing tag target and succeeds if it already points to requested `ref`.
  - Added detailed failure diagnostics with status/body excerpts from GitLab responses.

## MR !337

### Added
- New shared-library step `downloadConfluenceAttachments` in `vars/downloadConfluenceAttachments.groovy`.
  - Supports download by `PAGE_ID` or by `PAGE_NAME` + `SPACE` resolution.
  - Supports selective attachment download and rename via `ATTACHMENTS` (`String`, `List`, `Map`).
  - Adds `ALLOW_MISSING`, `OVERWRITE`, and `DEBUG` behavior controls.
  - Returns structured result map with `downloaded`, `skipped`, and `missing` collections.
- Step documentation for `downloadConfluenceAttachments` in `vars/downloadConfluenceAttachments.txt`.
- Unit tests for attachment download behavior in `src/test/groovy/vars/DownloadConfluenceAttachmentsTest.groovy`.
- New contributor guide in `CONTRIBUTING.md` with project patterns for `vars/`, docs, and test requirements.

### Changed
- Improved contribution standards by documenting repository conventions, validation approach, and Jenkins Pipeline Unit testing expectations.
